    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived `timezone` field to the owner response, mapping the locality/region to an IANA timezone name via the fixed table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane).\n\nChanges:\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `timezone` string property to the `OwnerDto` schema (right after `locality`), so the generated DTO has the field.\n- **`OwnerLocality.java`** \u2014 added a `REGION_TIMEZONE` table and a `timezoneForOwner(Owner)` helper that derives the region via the existing `forOwner(...)` locality logic and maps it to the IANA name (returns `null` for `UNKNOWN`/no known region).\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression populating `timezone` from `OwnerLocality.timezoneForOwner(owner)`.\n\nThis reuses the existing locality-derivation pipeline (postcode-first, then city table), so `timezone` stays consistent with `locality`. The acceptance test `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` (Sydney/NSW \u2192 `Australia/Sydney`) and the full suite pass.",
